(in-progress:)
  * Updating from an earlier version requires a game reset (-reset)
  * Updating also requires running "immortal-barons -set-dropfile" once:
    the door now needs to know which drop file your BBS writes, and will
    not start until it is set
  * PCBOARD.SYS and DORINFO1.DEF drop files are now supported, along
    with DOOR32.SYS and DOOR.SYS
  * An ally in a Full Defense Alliance now sends 30% of its mobile
    forces to help defend you
  * Desert regions earn more, matching the original game
  * Read Messages now shows one message at a time (Reply/Delete/Ignore/
    Quit), matching the original — Ignore keeps a message for next time,
    only Delete removes it
  * A Regular Attack captures more regions from a target whose net worth
    is spread thin over its land, and fewer from a dense, developed one

2026-07-24 (v0.0.2)
  * Winning a Regular Attack now lets you choose the types of the
    regions you capture (#58)
  * Winning a pirate raid that seizes land lets you choose its region
    types too (#21)
  * Combat reports now break down casualties by unit type for both
    the attacker and the defender
  * Pirate raids now happen randomly across turns (about 1 in 5)
    instead of all at once each day (#21)
  * The army now eats far less food, matching the original game — a
    large standing army is no longer food-crippling
  * Renamed the pirate factions to original names
  * Screens follow BRE more closely — highlighted figures, the news
    masthead/bulletin layout, and region-table colors
  * "Since your last play" events now show after you start your turn,
    not before the main menu
  * Windows door: works when the BBS hands over a non-blocking socket
    (MagicBBS) (#37)

2026-07-22
  * v0.0.1 released
